{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T07:27:50.682Z","ordinal":1941,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0be3b8594dbded3e016a952ce8dec087d1a5432e3b8e21b7e3","status":"completed","call_id":"call_HEi4m9qXFDso3JOBNNp8ZJSy","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /home/ubuntu/cd3-clean/CD3_OPTIMIZATION_REPORT.md\\n+# CD3 GH200 optimization follow-up (2026-08-31)\\n+\\n+All timings below use real Llama-3.1-70B layer 40 weights on GH200. Fused\\n+tables report P50 milliseconds with L2 flush and a concurrent H2D contender\\n+(10 warmups, 100 iterations). Every retained kernel passed correctness checks.\\n+\\n+## Retained changes\\n+\\n+- Standalone decoder: replace six scalar byte loads for each 48-bit code word\\n+  with two aligned 32-bit loads and a shift. The final chunk reads bytes\\n+  1528..1535 and remains inside the 1536-byte tile.\\n+- Fused selector: use split-K=2 for GateUp at N<=64. Existing choices remain\\n+  QKV=4 and O/Down=2; at N=128 QKV=4 and O/GateUp/Down=2.\\n+\\n+## Final fused comparison\\n+\\n+| Projection | N | P4Flat | CD3 | CD3 vs P4Flat |\\n+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n+| QKV | 64 | 0.141 | 0.146 | +3.4% |\\n+| QKV | 128 | 0.311 | 0.190 | -39.0% |\\n+| O | 64 | 0.121 | 0.127 | +5.0% |\\n+| O | 128 | 0.205 | 0.137 | -33.4% |\\n+| GateUp | 64 | 0.534 | 0.629 | +17.8% |\\n+| GateUp | 128 | 0.685 | 0.836 | +22.1% |\\n+| Down | 64 | 0.285 | 0.386 | +35.6% |\\n+| Down | 128 | 0.463 | 0.412 | -11.0% |\\n+| Projection sum | 64 | 1.081 | 1.288 | +19.1% |\\n+| Projection sum | 128 | 1.664 | 1.575 | -5.4% |\\n+\\n+P4Flat pads small-M N=128 QKV/O/Down to TileN=192, so those three N=128\\n+comparisons are not clean codec-only comparisons. GateUp uses the actual\\n+TileN=128 path in both codecs and remains the key N=128 signal.\\n+\\n+## Final-code exception-off upper bound\\n+\\n+The timing-only variant omits exception restoration and therefore produces\\n+incorrect values; it is only an upper bound. Compared with the correct final\\n+kernel before the GateUp split-K change:\\n+\\n+| Projection | N | Correct | Exception off | Reduction |\\n+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n+| QKV | 64 | 0.145 | 0.089 | 38.6% |\\n+| QKV | 128 | 0.189 | 0.110 | 41.8% |\\n+| O | 64 | 0.127 | 0.078 | 38.6% |\\n+| O | 128 | 0.136 | 0.087 | 36.0% |\\n+| GateUp | 64 | 0.665 | 0.411 | 38.2% |\\n+| GateUp | 128 | 0.833 | 0.526 | 36.9% |\\n+| Down | 64 | 0.385 | 0.233 | 39.5% |\\n+| Down | 128 | 0.411 | 0.266 | 35.3% |\\n+\\n+This includes exception entry loads, mask construction, atomics, and their\\n+barriers. It is not the achievable speedup of one isolated edit.\\n+\\n+## Nsight Compute profile\\n+\\n+| Case | Barrier stall | Long scoreboard | Short scoreboard | Wait | Tensor active | Achieved occupancy |\\n+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n+| O N64 | 20.78% | 14.77% | 14.50% | 15.81% | 8.74% | 12.00% |\\n+| GateUp N64 | 19.42% | 12.80% | 15.38% | 13.96% | 10.29% | 16.17% |\\n+| GateUp N128 | 21.72% | 14.92% | 11.47% | 13.42% | 16.63% | 12.14% |\\n+| Down N64 | 21.13% | 13.98% | 14.59% | 16.00% | 8.96% | 12.04% |\\n+\\n+N64 uses 80 registers/thread and is limited to three blocks/SM by 74.75 KiB\\n+dynamic shared memory. N128 uses 124 registers/thread but its 80.64 KiB\\n+dynamic shared memory already limits it to two blocks/SM. Thus 128 registers\\n+is not by itself the current N128 occupancy cliff.\\n+\\n+## Rejected register-A ping-pong\\n+\\n+The N64-only double-buffered register-A variant passed correctness, but raised\\n+register use from 80 to 117 and regressed every measured projection by 1-3%:\\n+QKV 0.145->0.147, O 0.127->0.130, GateUp 0.665->0.674, and Down\\n+0.385->0.395 ms. It was not retained or extended to N128.\\n+\\n+## Split-K sweep\\n+\\n+| Projection | N | split-1 | split-2 | split-4 | Selected |\\n+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\\n+| QKV | 64 | 0.220 | 0.147 | 0.147 | 4 |\\n+| QKV | 128 | 0.234 | 0.237 | 0.190 | 4 |\\n+| O | 64 | 0.191 | 0.127 | 0.133 | 2 |\\n+| O | 128 | 0.197 | 0.136 | 0.138 | 2 |\\n+| GateUp | 64 | 0.666 | 0.627 | 0.630 | 2 |\\n+| GateUp | 128 | 0.859 | 0.836 | 0.848 | 2 |\\n+| Down | 64 | 0.628 | 0.385 | 0.409 | 2 |\\n+| Down | 128 | 0.648 | 0.412 | 0.413 | 2 |\\n+\\n+## Standalone weight and KV results\\n+\\n+The aligned loader reduced average CD3 weight decode from 0.242 to 0.237 ms\\n+(about 2.1%). Per projection it measured 0.100/0.082/0.501/0.265 ms for\\n+QKV/O/GateUp/Down, versus P4Flat 0.096/0.080/0.479/0.249 ms.\\n+\\n+KV remained effectively decode-neutral: CD3 resident decode was 0.052 ms at\\n+1024 blocks and 0.088 ms at 2048 blocks. H2D+decode was 0.219 and 0.399 ms,\\n+versus P4Flat 0.256 and 0.443 ms. Both resident and staged results were\\n+bit-exact.\\n+\\n+## Artifacts\\n+\\n+- `final_2xu32_gate_sk2_vs_p4flat.csv`: final fused comparison\\n+- `original.csv`, `mask_only.csv`, `loader_only.csv`, `final.csv`: controlled\\n+  fused ablations\\n+- `exception_off.csv`: timing-only upper bound\\n+- `splitk1.csv`, `splitk2.csv`, `splitk4.csv`: split-K sweep\\n+- `profile_*.ncu-rep`: Nsight Compute reports\\n+- `standalone_weight_2xu32_vs_p4flat.log`: weight benchmark\\n+- `standalone_kv_2xu32_vs_p4flat.log`: KV benchmark\\n+- `CD3_FUSED_ABLATION_VARIANTS.patch`: benchmark-only compile variants,\\n+  including the deliberately incorrect exception-off mode and rejected\\n+  ping-pong mode; this patch is not applied to production source.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a056aa-052c-7ae3-8ceb-a34b64d726d9","create_time":1788161247.261379}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-31T07:27:50.688Z","ordinal":1942,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a05669-fc4c-7aa0-b9a1-034d833ed8ed","turn_id":"01a056aa-052c-7ae3-8ceb-a34b64d726d9","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-351368ff-8328-4420-b3e1-173c9fde9b96","changes":{"/home/ubuntu/cd3-clean/CD3_OPTIMIZATION_REPORT.md":{"type":"add","content":"# CD3 GH200 optimization follow-up (2026-08-31)\n\nAll timings below use real Llama-3.1-70B layer 40 weights on GH200. Fused\ntables report P50 milliseconds with L2 flush and a concurrent H2D contender\n(10 warmups, 100 iterations). Every retained kernel passed correctness checks.\n\n## Retained changes\n\n- Standalone decoder: replace six scalar byte loads for each 48-bit code word\n  with two aligned 32-bit loads and a shift. The final chunk reads bytes\n  1528..1535 and remains inside the 1536-byte tile.\n- Fused selector: use split-K=2 for GateUp at N<=64. Existing choices remain\n  QKV=4 and O/Down=2; at N=128 QKV=4 and O/GateUp/Down=2.\n\n## Final fused comparison\n\n| Projection | N | P4Flat | CD3 | CD3 vs P4Flat |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| QKV | 64 | 0.141 | 0.146 | +3.4% |\n| QKV | 128 | 0.311 | 0.190 | -39.0% |\n| O | 64 | 0.121 | 0.127 | +5.0% |\n| O | 128 | 0.205 | 0.137 | -33.4% |\n| GateUp | 64 | 0.534 | 0.629 | +17.8% |\n| GateUp | 128 | 0.685 | 0.836 | +22.1% |\n| Down | 64 | 0.285 | 0.386 | +35.6% |\n| Down | 128 | 0.463 | 0.412 | -11.0% |\n| Projection sum | 64 | 1.081 | 1.288 | +19.1% |\n| Projection sum | 128 | 1.664 | 1.575 | -5.4% |\n\nP4Flat pads small-M N=128 QKV/O/Down to TileN=192, so those three N=128\ncomparisons are not clean codec-only comparisons. GateUp uses the actual\nTileN=128 path in both codecs and remains the key N=128 signal.\n\n## Final-code exception-off upper bound\n\nThe timing-only variant omits exception restoration and therefore produces\nincorrect values; it is only an upper bound. Compared with the correct final\nkernel before the GateUp split-K change:\n\n| Projection | N | Correct | Exception off | Reduction |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| QKV | 64 | 0.145 | 0.089 | 38.6% |\n| QKV | 128 | 0.189 | 0.110 | 41.8% |\n| O | 64 | 0.127 | 0.078 | 38.6% |\n| O | 128 | 0.136 | 0.087 | 36.0% |\n| GateUp | 64 | 0.665 | 0.411 | 38.2% |\n| GateUp | 128 | 0.833 | 0.526 | 36.9% |\n| Down | 64 | 0.385 | 0.233 | 39.5% |\n| Down | 128 | 0.411 | 0.266 | 35.3% |\n\nThis includes exception entry loads, mask construction, atomics, and their\nbarriers. It is not the achievable speedup of one isolated edit.\n\n## Nsight Compute profile\n\n| Case | Barrier stall | Long scoreboard | Short scoreboard | Wait | Tensor active | Achieved occupancy |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| O N64 | 20.78% | 14.77% | 14.50% | 15.81% | 8.74% | 12.00% |\n| GateUp N64 | 19.42% | 12.80% | 15.38% | 13.96% | 10.29% | 16.17% |\n| GateUp N128 | 21.72% | 14.92% | 11.47% | 13.42% | 16.63% | 12.14% |\n| Down N64 | 21.13% | 13.98% | 14.59% | 16.00% | 8.96% | 12.04% |\n\nN64 uses 80 registers/thread and is limited to three blocks/SM by 74.75 KiB\ndynamic shared memory. N128 uses 124 registers/thread but its 80.64 KiB\ndynamic shared memory already limits it to two blocks/SM. Thus 128 registers\nis not by itself the current N128 occupancy cliff.\n\n## Rejected register-A ping-pong\n\nThe N64-only double-buffered register-A variant passed correctness, but raised\nregister use from 80 to 117 and regressed every measured projection by 1-3%:\nQKV 0.145->0.147, O 0.127->0.130, GateUp 0.665->0.674, and Down\n0.385->0.395 ms. It was not retained or extended to N128.\n\n## Split-K sweep\n\n| Projection | N | split-1 | split-2 | split-4 | Selected |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| QKV | 64 | 0.220 | 0.147 | 0.147 | 4 |\n| QKV | 128 | 0.234 | 0.237 | 0.190 | 4 |\n| O | 64 | 0.191 | 0.127 | 0.133 | 2 |\n| O | 128 | 0.197 | 0.136 | 0.138 | 2 |\n| GateUp | 64 | 0.666 | 0.627 | 0.630 | 2 |\n| GateUp | 128 | 0.859 | 0.836 | 0.848 | 2 |\n| Down | 64 | 0.628 | 0.385 | 0.409 | 2 |\n| Down | 128 | 0.648 | 0.412 | 0.413 | 2 |\n\n## Standalone weight and KV results\n\nThe aligned loader reduced average CD3 weight decode from 0.242 to 0.237 ms\n(about 2.1%). Per projection it measured 0.100/0.082/0.501/0.265 ms for\nQKV/O/GateUp/Down, versus P4Flat 0.096/0.080/0.479/0.249 ms.\n\nKV remained effectively decode-neutral: CD3 resident decode was 0.052 ms at\n1024 blocks and 0.088 ms at 2048 blocks. H2D+decode was 0.219 and 0.399 ms,\nversus P4Flat 0.256 and 0.443 ms. Both resident and staged results were\nbit-exact.\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- `final_2xu32_gate_sk2_vs_p4flat.csv`: final fused comparison\n- `original.csv`, `mask_only.csv`, `loader_only.csv`, `final.csv`: controlled\n  fused ablations\n- `exception_off.csv`: timing-only upper bound\n- `splitk1.csv`, `splitk2.csv`, `splitk4.csv`: split-K sweep\n- `profile_*.ncu-rep`: Nsight Compute reports\n- `standalone_weight_2xu32_vs_p4flat.log`: weight benchmark\n- `standalone_kv_2xu32_vs_p4flat.log`: KV benchmark\n- `CD3_FUSED_ABLATION_VARIANTS.patch`: benchmark-only compile variants,\n  including the deliberately incorrect exception-off mode and rejected\n  ping-pong mode; this patch is not applied to production source.\n"}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /home/ubuntu/cd3-clean/CD3_OPTIMIZATION_REPORT.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1788161270688,"completed_at_ms":1788161270688}}
